{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-562"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Event Catering and Other Food Service Activities - Operations Coordination"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev4 "562"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :services/catering-coordination
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:operational-efficiency :facility-safety :administrative-transparency]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :cateringops-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics false
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger]
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "CateringOpsAdvisor ⊣ Governor, real langgraph-clj StateGraph
 (langgraph.graph, cateringops.operation/build -- replaces the prior
 hand-written `cond` state machine that only claimed StateGraph
 orchestration in its docstring), append-only audit ledger
 (cateringops.store/ledger + append-ledger!, MemStore and a
 DatomicStore backed by langchain.db via langchain-store.core). A
 back-office OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor for event catering (booking/
 scheduling, delivery status, non-food supply, staff shift proposals,
 facility safety flags) -- not a food-safety/recipe/food-handling
 authority. Five ops, all `:effect :propose` only. Three HARD
 invariants (target-not-verified, effect-not-propose, scope-excluded
 EN+JA substring scan) gate every proposal; `:flag-safety-concern`
 phase-auto-commit is always false, so it always escalates via the
 compiled graph's `:request-approval` node (`interrupt-before`,
 checkpoint-based resume) regardless of rollout phase. Every commit/
 hold/approval-rejected decision lands in the append-only ledger -- the
 Advisor is now a real `Advisor` protocol + `MockAdvisor` (the
 pre-existing confidence-scoring functions are wired in for the first
 time, not dead code), and the test suite is real `clojure.test`
 `deftest`/`is` (16 tests / 90 assertions, `kbb -M:dev:test`) that
 can genuinely fail -- replacing a prior harness that printed
 'All tests passed! (16/16)' unconditionally regardless of outcome.
 Demo runnable end-to-end against both Store backends
 (`kbb -M:dev:run`)."}
